sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Op as Operator (host)
    participant C as Docker Compose
    participant I as openshell-init
    participant G as openshell-gateway
    participant D as Docker driver<br/>(via docker.sock)
    participant S as Supervisor container
    participant W as Workload container
    participant A as Agent<br/>(hermes gateway run)

    rect rgb(235, 242, 255)
    Note over Op,G: Per deployment — compose --profile harness up
    Op->>C: docker compose --profile harness up -d
    C->>I: run generate-certs
    I-->>C: JWT signing key + mTLS certs written to openshell-data, exit 0
    C->>G: start (after init completes)
    G->>G: open gateway.db, load signing key,<br/>bind 127.0.0.1:8080
    Op->>G: openshell gateway add http://127.0.0.1:8080
    end

    rect rgb(240, 250, 240)
    Note over Op,A: Per sandbox — openshell sandbox create
    Op->>G: sandbox create --from image --policy --provider<br/>--expose 8642 -- hermes gateway run
    G->>G: validate policy, record sandbox in gateway.db,<br/>mint launch-scoped JWT
    G->>D: provision sandbox
    D->>D: create channel volume, write launch token<br/>into its bootstrap material
    D->>W: create from harness image, network_mode=none,<br/>openshell-sandbox as PID 1, then start
    D->>D: stage supervisor bundle into<br/>supervisor-only volume (JWT, credentials)
    D->>S: create from supervisor image, host networking, then start
    S->>G: dial 127.0.0.1:8080 with launch JWT
    G-->>S: session bearer, policy, provider credentials
    W->>S: dial control.sock on the channel volume
    S-->>W: verify pinned identity, supply bearer
    W->>W: apply Landlock + seccomp, drop to sandbox UID
    W->>A: launch the command after -- as a child
    G->>G: sandbox Ready, register the --expose route
    end

    rect rgb(255, 245, 235)
    Note over A,G: Runtime — every outbound connection, default-deny
    A->>W: vss calls connect(host.openshell.internal:7777),<br/>stopped by seccomp before it leaves
    W->>S: /usr/bin/python3.13 wants<br/>host.openshell.internal:7777
    S->>S: matches the vss-backend grant (tcp)
    S-->>A: dials VSS HAProxy, relays the stream
    A->>W: the model client calls connect(api.anthropic.com:443),<br/>stopped the same way
    W->>S: /usr/bin/python3.13 wants<br/>api.anthropic.com:443
    S->>S: matches the anthropic grant (REST, POST /v1/**)<br/>and swaps the api_key placeholder for the real key
    S-->>A: dials the provider, relays the stream
    A->>W: any other host — or this host from<br/>a binary the grant does not name
    W->>S: forwarded the same way
    S--xA: no grant matches — denied
    end
